    {
      "title": "INDIA bloc vows to fight 'vote chori', reclaim Jantar Mantar protest site",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/politics/india-bloc-vows-to-fight-vote-chori-reclaim-jantar-mantar-protest-site-126101301226_1.html",
      "description": "Opposition leaders met at Rahul Gandhi's residence to discuss their campaign against alleged vote theft and vowed to challenge Jantar Mantar's removal as a designated protest site",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-13T17:58:41"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student group marches in Delhi, seeks release of detained CJP leaders",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/student-group-marches-in-delhi-seeks-release-of-detained-cjp-leaders-126101300537_1.html",
      "description": "Members of a student organisation took out a march from Connaught Place on Tuesday, demanding immediate release of detained Cockroach Janata Party (CJP) leaders and opposing the de-notification of Jantar Mantar as a designated protest site.\nThe protesters, associated with student organisation Disha, called on citizens -- particularly youths -- to gather at Connaught Place in large numbers, and \"reclaim Jantar Mantar\".\nCJP leaders Saurav Das, Ashutosh Ranka and Ajinkya Shinde were detained by Delhi Police on Tuesday morning while they were trying to enter Jantar Mantar.\nIn a post on X, CJP founder Abhijeet Dipke said several other member had also been picked up by police.\nMembers of Disha demanded immediate release of Ranka, Das and other CJP members, describing the protest march as a demand for justice.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-13T08:38:26"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dipke calls those opposing tricolour hoisting at Jantar Mantar 'traitors'",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/dipke-calls-those-opposing-tricolour-hoisting-at-jantar-mantar-traitors-126101300437_1.html",
      "description": "Dipke's remarks came after Delhi Police detained CJP's Ashutosh Ranka, Saurav Das, and Ajinkya Shinde-who had gathered at the Jantar Mantar earlier in the morning",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-13T07:02:59"
    },
    {
      "title": "CJP leaders Saurav Das, Ashutosh Ranka detained near Jantar Mantar",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/cjp-leaders-saurav-das-ashutosh-ranka-detained-near-jantar-mantar-126101300201_1.html",
      "description": "Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) leaders Saurav Das and Ashutosh Ranka were detained by Delhi Police on Tuesday while they were trying to reach Jantar Mantar, police sources said.\nIn a post on X, CJP founder Abhijeet Dipke said several other team members, including Ajinkya Shinde, had also been detained.\n\"Cockroaches with the Tiranga sneaked into Jantar Mantar early this morning before they were picked up by Delhi Police,\" Dipke said.\nHe said Ranka, Das, Shinde and other team members have been detained.\n\"You cannot denotify the resistance,\" he added, tagging Prime Minister Narendra Modi.\nDipke also shared a video that showed the CJP members jumping over a gate to enter Jantar Mantar and raising slogans like \"Bharat Mata ki Jai\". Police personnel are seen rushing and grabbing them.\nThe detentions come amid heightened security in New Delhi following calls for protests by different organisations against Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar over alleged irregularities in the Special",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-13T04:35:05"
    }
  ]
